 "_what": "Which level metrics sit on one side of price BY DEFINITION, as the stage's ENTRY_LEVEL_USUALLY_SKIPPED warning names them (\"The LONG entry level sits below price by definition, but a buy stop must rest above price, so this entry will be skipped on most bars\"). No hint, vocabulary entry or schema serves this, so it was swept: every price-unit metric with a legal `value` column was staged as BOTH levels of a STOP_THROUGH_LEVEL entry (levelOffsetAtrMultiple 0.2, validForBars 4; the level a plain reference - {rel: anchor}, offset 0, no knobs, no windowExtreme) on a create draft whose report reads it; a warning on entry.levels.LONG marks the metric `below`, one on entry.levels.SHORT `above`, none neither. Read by omega.trade_levels.entry_level_sides. Re-sweep when a re-extraction adds a price metric: a metric in neither `measured` nor `unmeasured` here is one this table has never seen.",
